 ## Limitations and Considerations
 
 - **Single-center experience.** Only one group (Rourke, University of Alberta) has described the technique, in 27 patients, and independent validation is lacking.<sup>[[1]](#ref1)</sup> The reported etiologies were LS (19), iatrogenic (5), or idiopathic (3); no separate post-hypospadias outcome was reported, so applicability after failed hypospadias repair remains uncertain.<sup>[[1]](#ref1)</sup>
-- **Stricture length.** Mean length was 3.2 cm (range 1–4 cm). In Morey's separate flap/graft onlay series, 10/11 isolated fossa strictures (1.5–2.5 cm) and 7/13 pendulous strictures extending into the fossa (4–16 cm) were successfully reconstructed; these data do not set a Sliding-T cutoff.<sup>[[9]](#ref9)</sup> For longer distal strictures, a subcoronal dorsal onlay (Favre: 16 patients, median length 5.5 cm, all stricture free at 41.5 months) or staged urethroplasty has been used.<sup>[[7]](#ref7)[[13]](#ref13)</sup>
